{"ts":"2026-06-15T01:14:34.732Z","type":"reply","reply":"Certainly, Commander.\n\nVerified:\nJarvis V5 doctrine is locked inside the Kingsmen repository.\nThe Jarvis HUD is now a repo surface, not a separate toy shell.\nThe native voice bridge posts heard speech into the Jarvis API and the evidence feed records the command.\n\nUnverified:\nAny live external status, deadline, portal condition, payment status, or official fact still requires live verification before execution.\n\nOperational meaning:\nJarvis is restored as a Commander-only command intelligence surface for briefing, inspection, repair, research, reporting, and governed tool routing.\n\nRisk:\nIf Windows speech recognition does not capture the microphone, the voice bridge will log the fault and the cockpit will show the failure instead of hiding it.\n\nRecommended command:\nSay “Jarvis”, then give one operational instruction such as “inspect Kingsmen health”, “repair this module”, or “give me the command brief”.\n\nStanding by, Sir.","intent":"brief","hash":"1f6dd35a39790eb73dac7e526b9a4f35973ba62a483fa9c419962792c64a8e70"}
